# The main menus (docs/plans/realm-ui.md, Phase 1): the home menu, About, the campaign picker, the
# Custom Game, Settings and Load / Save dialogs, and the in-game Game menu with its Quit and Exit
# popups (Save and quit saves in the autosave's slot, which Continue loads), in the three realms.
# Settings: every tab in each realm, Cancel, edits kept through a rebuild, Ok (checked with config.get; a script leaves the user configs
# alone) and Restore defaults. The profile (profile.set) picks the realm and fills the
# campaign row: none reached, campaign II reached, all three; Campaign resumes the campaign at its
# next mission, or opens the picker when more than one can be played, whose Continue starts the
# campaign picked; Continue loads the last save. Custom Game: realm rows (locked until their
# campaign is reached), map rows and the preview, the options, and Start of a preset game (Kambara)
# and of a blank one with options (Tampadesa), checking the session, a save and a load. Load /
# Save saves two games, reads their rows and preview, asks before overwriting, deletes one through
# its popup and loads the other. Each screen is checked for layout issues and saved as a screenshot
# under out/ui_menus/ (the CI artifact); Home, the picker, About, Custom Game, Settings and the Game
# menu at 200% and 75% UI scale too.
#
# The campaign's missions load the sample saves, so extract them first (unzip saves/sample_saves.zip,
# as CI does). The saves it writes (ui_menus, ui_menus_a, ui_menus_b, ui_menus_custom and the
# autosave, with their thumbnails) are deleted at the end. Save and quit writes saves/autosave.json,
# so the scenario stops at once if one is there: move a local autosave away before running it. Run
# it with --fresh-profile, as CI does, so it starts from an empty profile and leaves the local one
# alone:
#   cargo run -p HeritageBuilder -- --fresh-profile --script crates/game/tests/scenarios/ui_menus.jsonl
{"method": "time.fixed_dt", "params": {"dt": 0.016667}}
# Save and quit below overwrites the autosave and the end deletes it: refuse to run over one.
{"method": "assert.eq", "params": {"query": "session.save_info", "args": {"name": "autosave"}, "path": "/exists", "value": false}}
{"method": "assert.eq", "params": {"query": "session.state", "path": "/menus_mode", "value": "Home"}}
{"method": "input.move", "params": {"park": true}}
{"method": "wait.frames", "params": {"frames": 3}}

